{
 "about": "Live pictures for the worked-example calculators (tools upgrade 2026-10, docs/tools-upgrade-notes/anp-rest.md). One family per kind of formula, drawn by assets/tools/calculators.js from the calculator's own computed values: every key below is an input or derived key of that calculator (checked by scripts/test/anp-calc-pictures.test.mjs). Nothing here adds a number; the picture only shows what the formula already computed. tube: a vessel with an inlet and outlet gauge; its width follows radius r (a fraction of normal) or, failing that, resistance rRes as r = (default R / R)^(1/4); particles move at a speed proportional to flow / r^2 (velocity = flow / area). wave: an arterial pressure trace between diastolic and systolic, with MAP and the plain average as lines (the trace shape is schematic). balance: the pressures that push fluid out of and pull it into a capillary as arrows, and the net. pump: a ventricle filling to EDV and emptying to ESV (sv-ef), or beating at HR with SV per beat filling one minute's output (cardiac-output). stack: bars split into parts on one scale. Tool review 2026-11 added families drawn by assets/tools/calc-art.js (loaded on first use; its header lists them): trace, axon, regrow, burns, spun, smear, pool, score, snellen, ear, loud, gas, scale, calendar, surface, membrane, channel, sarcomere, lever, punnett, meiosis, count, sweat, bulb. Text fields (mode, label, title, cap, name, end, unit, tone, layout, foot, cls) are words, not keys; a cap's {key} prints that value.",
